{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JqMqnH31yCDMEP3TC9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I write, there's one thing to settle, plus a few questions.\n\n**The A1C claim.** I'd advise against saying the meals *will* lower someone's A1C, because your numbers don't back that up as a promise. Only 14 of your 88 customers shared results, and they chose to. One person's A1C went up. You also don't know who changed their medication during those three months. A skeptical reader, or a regulator looking at health claims, would spot that, and as a registered dietitian your credibility is the main thing you're selling. What the numbers do support is something like: *\"Of 14 customers who shared their A1C with me before starting and after three months, 10 saw it go down, by an average of 0.6 points across all 14.\"* It's honest, specific and still persuasive. (Can you confirm whether the 0.6 average is across all 14 or only the 10 whose A1C dropped?)\n\nMy questions:\n\n1. **Will you go with the honest version of the A1C result above instead of a promise?** If you'd like different wording, tell me what matters most to you.\n2. **Who reads this page, and how do they get there?** Is it mostly the person with diabetes, or a spouse or adult child buying for them? Do they come from doctor referrals, search, ads or word of mouth?\n3. **What do customers say about the food itself?** Do you have any quotes you're allowed to use, along with the cuisines or dishes people love most?\n4. **What are the practical details?** I need the delivery area, the order cutoff, whether people can pause or cancel anytime, any options for allergies or vegetarians, and how the meals arrive and are reheated.\n5. **What's your name, credential and business name, and what should the main button do?** For example: \"Start a $59 trial week.\"\n\nIf you don't know something, say so and I'll leave it out rather than guess."}],"contai