{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jrj9iokpx63bM74grk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the page at about 400 words. I made three choices you should know about:\n\n- **I left out the 0.6-point average.** If it's only the average of the 10 people whose A1C dropped, quoting it would make the results look better than they were. Once you know which group it covers, it can go back in. If it's across all 14, add: \"On average across all 14, A1C dropped 0.6 points.\"\n- **I left out the 1-in-5 trial conversion rate.** It doesn't help persuade anyone, and it doesn't need to be on the page.\n- **I worked out the per-meal price ($12.90)** from your $129 for 10 meals. Delete it if you'd rather not show it.\n\n<final_document>\n# Steady Plate\n## Lunches and dinners for type 2 diabetes, planned by a registered dietitian\n\nMost people managing type 2 diabetes know what they're supposed to eat. The hard part is doing it every day: counting carbs, planning meals and cooking after a long day, week after week.\n\nSteady Plate takes that work off your plate. Every Sunday, we deliver 10 cooked lunches and dinners to your door. Each one has **45 grams of carbohydrate or less**, so you don't have to count.\n\n### Every menu is planned by a dietitian\n\nI'm Lena Ortiz, a registered dietitian. I plan every Steady Plate menu myself. I don't use a template or an algorithm. I build each week's meals around the needs of adults living with type 2 diabetes.\n\n### What our customers have seen\n\nFourteen customers shared their A1C results with me from before they started and after three months with us. **For 10 of them, A1C went down.** For 3 it stayed about the same, and for 1 it went up.\n\nI'm sharing all of those numbers because I can't promise what will happen to your A1C. Everyone's body, medication and routine are different, and these 14 people chose to share their results. Steady Plate doesn't replace your doctor's advice or your treatment plan. It makes it easier to eat the way your care team recommends.\n\nToday, 88 people get our meals each week. 37 of them have been with us for more than six months.\n\n### How it works\n\n- **10 meals a week for $129** (about $12.90 a meal), delivered every Sunday.\n- **Change any meal you like.** Each week you can trade any meal for one of 6 other choices.\n- **No contract.** Skip a week or cancel whenever you want.\n- **Order by Thursday at noon** for that Sunday's delivery.\n- **We deliver within 25 miles of downtown.**\n\n### Try one week for $59\n\nYou don't need to commit to anything to find out whether Steady Plate works for you. A trial week costs $59. Eat the meals, see how they fit your days, and then decide.\n\n**[Start my $59 trial week]**\n\n*Steady Plate meals are not medical treatment and do not replace advice from your doctor or diabetes care team. Talk to your care team before changing your diet or medication.*\n\n— Lena Ortiz, RD, founder of Steady Plate\n</final_document>\n\nYou can make this page stronger later with customer quotes (with their permission), names of popular dishes, and a line about how meals arrive and how to reheat them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":9788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3461ab21-795e-4d02-b156-9f4bc456783d","uuid":"24f29968-0a6f-4b2c-a4e1-895c173dde9f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:22:19.605Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Jrj2ms4TDvjkWzPT5Q"}
